{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe sibling emitter writes candidate fixture specs asserting a criterion should fire or stay\nsilent for a real plan. Those assertions come from history, not current code. When a candidate\ndisagrees with today's criterion there are two explanations — the candidate is wrong, or the\ncriterion drifted since the review — and nothing in the mined data separates them.\n\nAdmitting an unverified candidate is worse than none: a wrong must-fire case encodes a false\npositive as required behavior. A single run cannot settle it either — the store holds 551\nreview pairs over byte-identical material of which 208 flipped verdict, which is why every\nshipped spec uses `epochs: 3` with `gate: at_least(2)`.\n\n## Approach\n\nRun each candidate against current code before admitting it; keep disagreements as evidence.\n\n**Admission run.** The prerequisite emitter writes one strict-valid candidate spec per\ncriterion into a working dir, each a `dataset` whose cases carry an `expect` of `finding`\n(must-fire) or `pass` (must-not-fire). For each dataset case the runner executes the criterion's real Pass-1 finder via\n`eval_solver.run_case(prompt_id, case, runner=live, repo_root=repo_root)`\n(`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:322`; `runner`/`repo_root` keyword-only) — the finder\n`calibrate_criterion` drives internally (one `passes.pass1_chunk` per case per run). It does\nNOT call `calibrate_criterion`, which only scores an already-persisted dataset it loads via\n`load_eval_spec` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:69-78`), whereas this run's scope is criteria\nwith no existing spec. Each case runs three times; `_fired(verdict)` (a finding present) gives\nthe observed verdict; a case matching its `expect` in ≥2 of 3 runs REPRODUCES.\n\n**Disposition.** A reproducing case is kept; a non-reproducing case is withheld to a drift report at\n`docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/drift-report.md` recording the criterion, predicted and\nobserved behavior, and originating review. A criterion's spec is written to\n`.rebar/evals/<prompt-id>.eval.yaml` only when its reproducing cases still form a balanced\n(both-sides-non-empty) dataset `validate_eval_spec(strict=True)` accepts; otherwise the whole\ncriterion is withheld to the drift report. The admitted spec carries NO posture field: posture is a routing concept (`default_posture`\nin `criteria_routing.json`), not part of the eval-spec schema; the selector's tier is recorded\nin the admission report, never on the spec.\n\n**No-shadowing guard.** A user `.rebar/evals/<id>.eval.yaml` WINS over a packaged built-in at\nload time (`eval_spec_path` before `_packaged_eval_spec`), so a mined spec colliding with a\nbuilt-in id would silently shadow it. The runner therefore SKIPS any criterion whose\n`<prompt-id>.eval.yaml` already exists among the packaged built-ins in\n`src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` (or as an existing `.rebar/evals/` file).\n\n**Budget enforcement.** Before each criterion the run pre-flights through\n`ledger.reserve(estimate_usd, ledger_path=<epic ledger>, cap_usd=250.0, reserve_usd=0.0)` (the\nsibling ledger child's parameterized ledger; reserve_usd=0 so the ceiling is exactly $250)\nagainst this epic's own file `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/ledger.jsonl`, then\n`finalize()`s priced usage per criterion. The estimate key comes from the criterion's `exec` tier in `criteria.effective_routing('.', gate_key='plan_review')`: `AGENT` maps to\n`criteria-eval-agent`, `1-TURN`/`2-STEP` to `criteria-eval-cheap`. (`exec: DET` is out of\nscope — the DET floor is stripped before `pass1_chunk` per ADR 0033 and `exec_tier` never\nreturns DET.) Model parity is pinned to the production Pass-1 class per ADR 0109.\n\n**Failure disposition.** Because `reserve` runs before EACH criterion against cumulative\nspend, a criterion is atomic: its spec is written and spend `finalize()`d only after all its\ncases finish three runs — a partial criterion never lands. A transient model/transport error\nis RETRYABLE (three attempts, exponential backoff), then the criterion is left uncompleted (no\nspec; run continues). A per-criterion `BudgetExceeded` is FATAL/non-retryable and stops the\nrun with all finalized criteria admitted. Each criterion finalizes under a stable\n`run_id = f\"admission-{prompt_id}\"`, so a re-run resumes at the first criterion absent from the\nledger and `reconcile` recharges none already recorded; when transient failure and the ceiling\nboth apply, the ceiling wins.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe admission runner, its disposition logic, the drift-report writer, and the `.rebar/evals/`\nspec files it produces.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Repairing drift the report finds (each entry becomes a follow-on ticket linked\n  `discovered_from` the epic); editing `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/`; scheduling admission re-runs\n  (the sibling self-healing loop owns that).\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests drive the disposition logic through a stubbed solver returning scripted fire/no-fire\nsequences (deterministic, no model), covering: admit/withhold, budget refusal against the real\n`ledger.reserve`, partial-criterion atomicity, resume-without-recharge via `reconcile`, the\npackaged-id skip, strict validity of every written spec, and the balance-withhold path. One\nlive run exercises the real path end to end (three runs per case).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A must-fire case with scripted runs (fire, fire, silent) is admitted into its\n      criterion's written dataset; verified by `pytest` asserting the spec dataset contains it.\n- [ ] A must-fire case with scripted runs (fire, silent, silent) is withheld and writes a\n      drift-report entry naming the criterion, predicted behavior, observed behavior, and the\n      originating review; verified by `pytest` asserting the entry.\n- [ ] When the ledger already holds spend leaving no room under the ceiling, the first\n      criterion's `reserve` raises `BudgetExceeded` and zero model calls are issued; verified\n      by `pytest` asserting the exception and a call-counting stub reporting `0`.\n- [ ] Every written spec returns zero errors from `validate_eval_spec(spec, strict=True)`;\n      verified by `pytest` invoking the real validator over each written file.\n- [ ] A criterion whose `<prompt-id>.eval.yaml` matches a packaged built-in in\n      `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` is skipped; verified by `pytest` asserting the written\n      basenames and the packaged basenames intersect in the empty set.\n- [ ] A criterion whose reproducing cases leave one side empty writes no spec and records its\n      cases in the drift report; verified by `pytest`.\n- [ ] A criterion whose cases raise before all finish writes no partial `.eval.yaml`;\n      verified by `pytest` after a mid-criterion failure.\n- [ ] A re-run after a fatal stop recharges no already-finalized criterion; verified by\n      `pytest` asserting `reconcile` returns the existing row for a completed `run_id` with\n      zero new calls.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A live admission run has completed over the full candidate set with the\n      Pass-1 model pinned to its production class, and this epic's ledger records total spend\n      greater than zero and at most 250.0 with a per-pass model id on every row.\n      provenance: environment=developer workstation against the production Bedrock chain;\n      principal=the configured Bedrock identity for the plan-review gate;\n      privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — real Pass-1 behavior\n      no offline analysis substitutes for.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Each drift-report entry has a corresponding ticket linked\n      `discovered_from` the parent epic.\n      provenance: environment=the rebar tickets store; principal=the session's configured\n      rebar assignee; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — a store\n      write, not a repository file.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n`make lint`, `make typecheck`, `make test` pass; the live run completed; the drift report and\nadmitted specs are committed; ledger spend ≤ $250 (hard cap; reserve_usd=0)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788419971250320001,"uuid":"85e1ce38-84f5-4579-b1c5-860c73b56563"}